[size=6]SkyLink AI[/size]

SkyLink AI is an SKSE plugin and MCP server that gives AI assistants direct, real-time access to Skyrim's engine. Ask Claude to check your inventory, change the weather, play an animation, look up a quest, or spawn an enemy — and it just does it, live in your game.

[size=5]What this is NOT... and what it could be[/size]

This is NOT a replacement for in-game AI packages for NPCs or Creatures. This is NOT an AI that plays the game for you. This is NOT something that requires an expensive AI subscription.

Think of SkyLink AI as a [b]Help Desk[/b] for your game. Ask the AI what it can do, how it can help you. Play around with it.

[size=4]FAQ[/size]

[b]Does this cost money / burn tokens?[/b]
No paid subscription required. Works with free Claude accounts, local models via Ollama, or any MCP-compatible AI client. You can run a lightweight local AI on your own hardware and pay nothing.

[b]Does this control NPCs or replace their AI?[/b]
No. It doesn't modify NPC AI packages, dialogue, or behavior. It's a utility — it reads and acts on game state through the SKSE engine. You can manage idle animations, move NPCs, check their stats, but you're not replacing Radiant AI.

[b]Can this crash my game?[/b]
The tool includes a safety checker that detects risky states (loading, kill moves, saves) before executing commands. Teleporting during active combat can occasionally cause crashes from animation mods like OAR — the same thing that happens with fast travel or console coc commands.

