[/list]

[size=5]What is MCP?[/size]

The [url=https://modelcontextprotocol.io/]Model Context Protocol[/url] is an open standard that lets AI assistants call external tools. SkyLink AI exposes 74 Skyrim tools through MCP, so Claude Desktop (or any MCP-compatible client) can read and modify your game state through natural conversation.

[size=5]What Can It Do? (74 Tools)[/size]

[b]Player[/b]
[list]
[*]Stats, skills, level, perks, spells, shouts, active effects[/*]
[*]Inventory management (view, add, remove, equip)[/*]
[*]Appearance and faction membership[/*]
[*]Character blueprint export (full build snapshot to JSON)[/*]
[*]God mode, immortal mode, collision toggle[/*]
[/list]

[b]World[/b]
[list]
[*]Weather control, time of day[/*]
[*]Teleportation, cell info, nearby objects[/*]
[*]Doors, locks, containers, loot scanning[/*]
[*]Map marker discovery[/*]
[*]Merchant inventories and bounties[/*]
[/list]

[b]NPCs[/b]
[list]
[*]Nearby NPC detection, detailed info, crosshair targeting[/*]
[*]Follower management and detection state[/*]
[*]Play/stop idle animations (native API — works with all mods including ESL-flagged plugins)[/*]
[*]Move, kill, set relationships[/*]
[/list]

[b]Quests[/b]
[list]
[*]Quest info, stages, objectives, aliases, quest items[/*]
[*]Set stage, start/stop/complete quests[/*]
[*]Quest variable reading[/*]
[/list]

[b]Combat[/b]
[list]
[*]Combat state, damage stats, threat assessment[/*]
[*]Real-time hit events with attacker/target role identification (player, follower, other)[/*]
[/list]

[b]Utility[/b]
[list]
[*]Form search engine (replaces the console help command — searches 30+ form types)[/*]
[*]Console command execution with output capture[/*]
[*]Papyrus VM bridge — call any mod's Papyrus functions at runtime[/*]
[*]Music playback and volume control[/*]
[*]Screenshot capture, save/load game[/*]
[*]Event system (17 event types: combat, death, quests, location changes, and more)[/*]
[*]SKSE plugin config read/write (SmoothCam, po3_Tweaks, etc.)[/*]
[*]Load order and mod detection[/*]
[/list]

