[size=5]Requirements[/size]

[list]
[*]Skyrim SE or AE — Steam 1.7.104 (SKSE64 2.3.1), 1.6.1130–1.6.1170, or SE 1.5.97[/*]
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download/dotnet/10.0].NET 10 Runtime[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://claude.ai/download]Claude Desktop[/url] (or any MCP-compatible AI client)[/*]
[/list]

[size=5]Installation[/size]

1. Extract the Data folder into your Skyrim directory (or install via MO2 / Vortex)
2. Install .NET 10 Runtime if not already installed
3. Add the following to your Claude Desktop config (%APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json):

[code]{
  "mcpServers": {
    "skyrim": {
      "command": "dotnet",
      "args": ["<SKYRIM_PATH>\\Data\\SKSE\\Plugins\\SkyLinkAI_Server\\SkyrimMCP.dll"]
    }
  }
}[/code]

4. Launch Skyrim via SKSE, open Claude Desktop, and start talking to your game.

[size=4]How It Works[/size]

[code]Claude Desktop <--MCP/stdio--> .NET MCP Server <--named pipe--> SKSE Plugin (inside Skyrim)[/code]

The SKSE plugin runs inside Skyrim's process and exposes game state over a named pipe. The .NET MCP server translates between Claude's MCP protocol and the plugin. All game interactions use native CommonLibSSE-NG API calls wherever possible — only 3 operations fall back to console commands where no native API exists.

